                        "review": "[i]Game Breaking Bugs Included[/i]\r\n\r\nShould be a neutral score; but that doesn't exist.\r\n\r\nAs the title states there are game breaking bugs still present in this game all these years later. When they occur the game essentially forces you the alt+f4. There were times I could play for a while without encountering it; if you don't play too quickly once it becomes your turn that seems to weirdly help. \r\n\r\nThe gameplay itself is decent and the story elements of character dialog are well themed. Card balance could definitely be better as there are a handful that completely outclass everything else. Once you figure them out you basically have one deck to destroy everything. I would have preferred two sided interaction during a turn; instead the opponent cannot interact with what you are doing outside of what has already been played on the field. Lastly, the main campaign does feel like it drags on too long because the enemy deck variety really falls off around the half way point. \r\n\r\nIf it wasn't for the major bugs, I could recommend but it’s a little too precarious as it currently stands.",
